## 2. First run — the order that matters

1. **Profile Manager** — create `SBI_PREPROD`. Enter Teller ID, teller password,
   the new password used by transaction 9750, checker credentials and the CBS
   reset string. All of it is encrypted at rest and masked everywhere.
2. **Record Transaction 9750 first.** It is the forced Change Password screen and
   is auto-attached as a pre-step to every other transaction. Record it once; if
   SBI ever changes that screen, re-record only 9750 and every transaction
   benefits.
3. **Record your business transaction** (e.g. 400, 1045). Perform it normally in
   the Edge window the platform opens. Stop, then **Keep or Discard**.
4. **Test Data Editor** — fill in the banking values. The platform never invents
   CIF, PAN, account numbers, branch codes or IDs.
5. **Execute** — pick transaction + environment + profile, run, watch live status.
6. **Reports Dashboard** — drill into any run.

