## 3. What a recording captures

A recording is a full digital twin, not a click log:

- every page: full DOM, rendered HTML, URL, title, frames/iframes, shadow roots
- **every interactable element on every page** — not only what you clicked, so a
  future BRD can reference an element you never touched
- a ranked multi-strategy locator repository per element
  (`id → name → data-* → aria → css → relative XPath → placeholder → text →
  class → absolute XPath`)
- DOM snapshots before/after every action, plus a structural diff
- screenshots before/after every action
- the workflow path (`Login → Dashboard → CIF Creation → Review → Confirmation`)
- input **metadata only** — never raw values (Section 7)
- validation rules and every error / warning / success message
- optional network activity (URLs, status codes, timings)

Every re-recording creates a **new version**. Nothing is ever overwritten.

